// The raw shape of every icon in the app.
//
// AUTO-GENERATED from lucide-react's node data, so the geometry is lucide's own —
// do not hand-edit the paths. Each entry is a list of SVG child elements with their
// attributes, which AnimatedIcon renders into an <svg> at runtime.
//
// Why the icons are inlined as data rather than imported from lucide-react: only
// the icons actually used are carried (the full library is thousands), nothing is
// fetched at runtime, and — the real reason — each child element can be given an
// individual class (`ai-p0`, `ai-p1`, …) so CSS can animate the PARTS of an icon
// independently. That is what lets the padlock's shackle lift on its own, the
// archive lid open, and the undo arrow's head pull back (see icons.css).
//
// TO ADD AN ICON: copy its node array from lucide, add an entry here, add the
// matching kebab-case name to KEBAB below, export it from AnimatedIcon.tsx, and —
// optionally — give it a hover animation in icons.css. Nothing else is needed.
export type IconNode = [tag: string, attrs: Record<string, string | number>];

